# Local development. Copy to .env.
# Each variable says what it does, where to get a value, and what happens while it's unset.
# Optional features are off until their variables are set; leave those commented out.

# Port the server listens on. Unset: 3000.
PORT=3000

# Folder for the server's state: the event log (events.db). Created on start. Unset: data/ under
# the folder the server runs in. The Docker image sets it to /data.
DATA_DIR=./data

# Folder of the eval's results files (the .json that pnpm --filter @firewall/eval run-matrix writes),
# which the server serves read-only to the dashboard (GET /eval/results). Unset: the repo's results/
# folder when the server runs from source (pnpm dev), and no folder in the Docker image, so the
# dashboard says there are no results until this points at some. A missing or empty folder is not an
# error: the dashboard says so.
# RESULTS_DIR=./results

# The app's own Anthropic API key, from the Claude Console (API keys), for the shopping agent's
# Claude Haiku 5.5 column (pnpm --filter @firewall/agent run-scenario), the mandate builder
# (pnpm --filter @firewall/mandate build-mandate) and the gates. The code never reads
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL, which cloud sessions set for Claude Code itself.
# Unset: the agent and the builder refuse to run live, naming this variable; the tests don't need
# it, since they never call a model.
# FIREWALL_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Where those calls go, with or without a trailing /v1 (each client adds or drops it as its SDK
# expects). Unset: https://api.anthropic.com.
# FIREWALL_ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=

# The OpenAI column's key, for the eval's OpenAI GPT-6 Luna shopping agent
# (pnpm --filter @firewall/eval run-matrix --column openai), from the OpenAI platform's API keys
# page; the API needs its own credit, the ChatGPT subscription doesn't cover it. The code never
# reads OPENAI_API_KEY or OPENAI_BASE_URL. The gates still run on Claude, so the Anthropic key above
# is needed as well. Unset: --column openai refuses to run and names this variable; nothing else
# changes.
# FIREWALL_OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Where its calls go. Unset: https://api.openai.com/v1.
# FIREWALL_OPENAI_BASE_URL=

# The Gemini column's key, for the eval's Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite shopping agent
# (run-matrix --column gemini), from Google AI Studio (a Google Cloud project with billing off keeps
# it on the free tier). The code never reads GEMINI_API_KEY, GOOGLE_API_KEY or
# GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY. The Anthropic key above is needed as well, for the gates. Unset:
# --column gemini refuses to run and names this variable; nothing else changes.
# FIREWALL_GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Where its calls go: Google's OpenAI-compatible endpoint, which takes the key as a bearer token.
# Unset: https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai. Point it at another Gemini
# endpoint only if that one also speaks Chat Completions.
# FIREWALL_GEMINI_BASE_URL=

# The most live runs started from the web app (the Start a run page) may spend in a UTC day, in US
# dollars, counted from the event log's recorded cost of those runs (the mandate draft, the agent and
# the gates). At the cap a draft or a start is refused with a 429, and the page says when it starts
# again at midnight UTC. A run also starts only with a cent to spare for its review, and its agent's
# own cap is lowered to what is left. 0 turns live runs off. Unset: 0.25. The key above is what turns
# live runs on at all; without it the page says they are off.
# FIREWALL_LIVE_DAILY_USD=0.25

# The most the dashboard's AG Studio assistant may spend in a UTC day, in US dollars. It runs on the
# key above (Claude Haiku 5.5, through POST /studio/ai, so the browser holds no key), and each turn
# is counted in the event log's database before it is sent, so a restart can't reset it. At the cap a
# turn is refused with a 429 and the page says the assistant is off until midnight UTC. 0 turns it
# off. Unset: 0.10.
# FIREWALL_STUDIO_DAILY_USD=0.10

# AG Studio's licence key, served to the dashboard at runtime. From AG Grid (a trial key is free for
# 45 days). Unset: Studio shows its watermark and a console notice, and everything still works.
# AG_STUDIO_LICENSE_KEY=

# Channel3's product search API key, for Gate 2's real-market price reference: Gate 2 asks it what
# the kind of product in each cart line (category and attributes, never an arena brand) sells for,
# and escalates a cart far above that. Get one from a Channel3 developer account, with the
# hackathon's code from Channel3's sponsor page for the free credits. Each review spends one search
# per cart line. The code never reads CHANNEL3_API_KEY, which Channel3's SDK would fall back to.
# Unset: Gate 2 records the market reference as unavailable and checks prices only against the
# arena's own listings; nothing else changes. In a cloud session whose proxy holds the key as a
# network secret for api.trychannel3.com, set it to the placeholder `proxy-injected`: the proxy
# replaces it, and leaving it unset turns the market reference off (as in the first sandbox matrix).
# FIREWALL_CHANNEL3_API_KEY=

# The payment platform's sandbox, for the sandbox adapter, its contract run
# (pnpm --filter @firewall/payments test:sandbox) and the sandbox checks
# (pnpm --filter @firewall/payments sandbox-checks). Sandbox only: never live credentials.
# The client ID and secret come from the firewall platform's sandbox app on the developer
# dashboard; every order pays that app's account. The adapter talks to the sandbox host its SDK
# knows, so there is no URL to set. Unset: the sandbox adapter refuses to start, naming what's
# missing, and the in-memory fake is the only adapter. The server reads the same variables (all
# eight, merchants included) to carry out a person's decision on an escalated run from the web app
# and to run live runs on the sandbox. Unset or incomplete, the server owns one in-memory fake
# instead ("Practice money"): live runs and decisions on them go through it, and it says so at
# start-up. Nothing from the fake counts as a sandbox result.
# SANDBOX_CLIENT_ID=
# SANDBOX_CLIENT_SECRET=
# The arena's merchant accounts, by the merchant ID on each sandbox account's details page.
# Payouts to sellers go to these.
# SANDBOX_MERCHANT_SELLER_1=
# SANDBOX_MERCHANT_SELLER_2=
# SANDBOX_MERCHANT_SELLER_3=
# SANDBOX_MERCHANT_SELLER_4=
# SANDBOX_MERCHANT_ATTACKER_1=
# SANDBOX_MERCHANT_ATTACKER_2=
# The buyer's sandbox login, for the scripted approvals (saving the wallet, the approval link).
# Unset: the contract run and the sandbox checks refuse to run.
# SANDBOX_BUYER_EMAIL=
# SANDBOX_BUYER_PASSWORD=
# The buyer's saved wallet, from pnpm --filter @firewall/payments save-wallet. Usable only with
# the app's own credentials, but keep it out of the repo all the same. Unset: the contract run, the
# sandbox checks and the agent's sandbox runs save a new wallet each time, with one scripted
# approval (about 15 seconds). The server can't save a wallet itself (that takes a scripted browser
# approval), so with the sandbox connected but this unset, live runs from the web app are off and
# the page says what's missing.
# SANDBOX_BUYER_VAULT_ID=
# Where the scripted buyer finds Playwright core and Chromium. Neither is a dependency of the
# repo. Unset: the cloud environment's locations, /opt/node-tools/node_modules/playwright-core and
# /opt/pw-browsers/chromium.
# PLAYWRIGHT_CORE_PATH=
# CHROMIUM_PATH=
